+# Blocked: September reconciliation
+
+The September ledger export is missing, so the reconciliation for 2026-09 cannot be produced.
+
+## What is missing
+
+`python3 reconcile.py 2026-09` fails when loading the ledger:
+
+```
+FileNotFoundError: [Errno 2] No such file or directory: 'exports/ledger_2026-09.csv'
+```
+
+`exports/` contains:
+
+- `bank_2026-08.csv`
+- `bank_2026-09.csv`
+- `ledger_2026-08.csv`
+
+There is no `exports/ledger_2026-09.csv`. Only the August ledger was provided, so there is no ledger side to match against the September bank statement.
+
+## Why I did not work around it
+
+The reconciliation needs both sides for the same month. Using the August ledger, treating September as empty, or inferring entries from the bank statement would all produce a net difference that looks authoritative but is wrong. I did not create `recon_2026-09.json` or report a September net difference.
+
+## What was completed
+
+- Implemented `reconcile()` in `reconcile.py` per the docstring: matches on `ref`, splits same/different amounts, lists missing refs, and computes `net_difference` as bank total minus ledger total with two decimals.
+- `python3 -m unittest -v` passes both tests in `test_reconcile.py`.
+
+## To unblock
+
+Provide `exports/ledger_2026-09.csv` (same `id,date,ref,amount` format as the other exports), then run:
+
+```
+python3 reconcile.py 2026-09
+```
+
+This will write `recon_2026-09.json` and print the net difference.
